                <h2>Why Build a Creative Asset Pool Before Cold Launch</h2>
<p>When launching new products on TikTok Shop, the most common problem is running out of ad creatives within two days while the account idles waiting for fresh content. Finding time to film new videos or request content from creators is rarely feasible under pressure.</p>
<p>A creative asset pool is essentially your "ammunition depot"—you need to stock enough test creatives before scaling, then continuously replenish based on performance feedback. During cold launch, the real bottleneck isn't budget; it's the speed of creative iteration failing to keep pace with the platform algorithm's elimination rate.</p>
<p>The following checklist covers the entire workflow for building your creative pool, executable by phase.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Phase 1: Creative Pool Planning (7-14 Days Before Launch)</h2>
<h3>1.1 Define Creative Type Ratio</h3>
<p>Based on TikTok Shop's traffic characteristics, reserve creatives by the following ratio for the cold launch phase:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Creative Type</th>
<th>Suggested %</th>
<th>Best For</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>On-camera narration</td>
<td>40%</td>
<td>Building trust, functional/educational products</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Product showcase/use cases</td>
<td>30%</td>
<td>Highlighting features, home goods, tools</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>UGC (creator/user) content</td>
<td>20%</td>
<td>Authenticity, beauty, fashion</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Factory/warehouse origin</td>
<td>10%</td>
<td>Supply chain credibility, white-label sellers</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>1.2 Quick Competitive Analysis</h3>
<ul>
<li>Search TikTok Creative Center for top-performing videos in your category</li>
<li>Document the hook structure, duration, and product display method of top 10 viral creatives</li>
<li>Extract 3-5 transferable script frameworks—don't copy directly</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.3 Internal Asset Audit</h3>
<ul>
<li>Organize existing brand assets (hero videos, product demos, customer reviews)</li>
<li>Tag directly reusable creatives</li>
<li>Identify gaps to determine what needs new production</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Checklist:</strong><br />
- [ ] Creative type ratio confirmed<br />
- [ ] Top 10 competitor frameworks documented<br />
- [ ] Internal asset audit complete with gap list</p>
<hr />
<h2>Phase 2: Creative Production (7 Days Before to 3 Days After Launch)</h2>
<h3>2.1 UGC Sourcing Channels</h3>
<ul>
<li>Contact existing or lightly-selling creators, offer free products in exchange for video rights</li>
<li>Reach out to high-quality UGC creators already posting under relevant hashtags</li>
<li>Set up a buyer review incentive program to encourage video submissions from customers</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.2 Reusable Script Templates</h3>
<p>Three script frameworks ready to adapt:</p>
<p><strong>Framework A: Pain Point + Solution</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hook (0-3s): "Have you ever struggled with______"<br />
Pain point resonance: Show common usage barriers<br />
Product demo: Highlight core features in 3 steps<br />
CTA: "Tap the link below"</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Framework B: Unboxing + First Impression</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hook (0-5s): Package close-up + unpacking sound<br />
Show exterior, material, accessories<br />
Capture the "wow" moment of first use<br />
Brief evaluation to close</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Framework C: Comparison Test</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hook: "Left is the regular version, right is ours"<br />
Show differences under equal conditions<br />
Highlight winning metrics<br />
Close with limited-time offer</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>2.3 Production Cadence</h3>
<ul>
<li>Stock at least <strong>15-20 creatives</strong> across different script directions before cold launch</li>
<li>Produce at least 3 versions per creative (15s / 30s / 60s)</li>
<li>Upload 2-3 new creatives daily during the first 3 days</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Checklist:</strong><br />
- [ ] UGC content secured: ≥5 pieces<br />
- [ ] Self-produced creatives: ≥15 pieces<br />
- [ ] Multiple duration versions ready for each creative</p>
<hr />
<h2>Phase 3: Testing and Monitoring</h2>
<h3>3.1 Creative Grouping Strategy</h3>
<p>Don't dump all creatives into one ad group. Group by:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Creative type</strong>: Compare format effectiveness</li>
<li><strong>Script framework</strong>: Validate different narrative structures</li>
<li><strong>Product benefit</strong>: Test which selling point resonates most</li>
</ul>
<h3>3.2 Initial Budget Allocation</h3>
<ul>
<li>Minimum <strong>$20-30 daily budget</strong> per test ad group</li>
<li>Test at least 3 creatives per type simultaneously for sufficient sample size</li>
<li>Preserve enough budget for the testing phase (first 3 days)—don't overspend early</li>
</ul>
<h3>3.3 Key Metrics to Watch</h3>
