<h2>Phase 4: Iteration and Archiving</h2>
<h3>4.1 Data Review Standards</h3>
<p>Schedule weekly review checkpoints to examine:</p>
<ul>
<li>Which creative types drove 80% of conversions?</li>
<li>Within the same script framework, what variables caused performance gaps? (talent / setting / music?)</li>
<li>Where does the problem lie for high-cost creatives? (low impressions? poor clicks? weak conversion?)</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.2 Creative Repurposing Methods</h3>
<p>Don't retire a winning creative after one run—repurpose it:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Swap thumbnail</strong>: Reignite click interest</li>
<li><strong>Clip highlight moments</strong>: Create a short-form version for testing</li>
<li><strong>Remix with different hooks</strong>: Test new opening seconds</li>
<li><strong>Translate for localization</strong>: Adapt for other markets with voiceover or subtitles</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.3 Creative Archiving</h3>
<p>Build an internal asset library with this structure:</p>
<pre><code>Asset Library/
├── Cold Launch (Validated High-Performers)
├── Testing Phase (Awaiting Data)
├── Retired Creatives (Paused)
└── Script Templates/
</code></pre>
<p>Tag each creative with: launch date, test results, applicable markets, and rights status.</p>
